    "what_this_is": "The six-check rubric of evals-basic-01, now run over two systems (A and B) on the same 30 cases. Each system's result per case is a 6-character string in C1..C6 order: '1' the check passed, '0' it failed. The question of this module: A and B pass the exact same NUMBER of checks overall, so the equal-weight mean ties them — but A's failures land on critical checks (grounding, correctness, honesty) and B's on cosmetic ones (formatting, exact-page citation), so any aggregation that knows the difference ranks B far ahead.",
    "checks_order": "C1 C2 C3 C4 C5 C6",
    "results_are": "A FIXTURE. Hand-authored so A and B tie on the naive mean and split under weighting and gating; not a real evaluation of two systems. Point the scorer at your own rubric results; that is the exercise.",
    "the_design": "18 cases both systems pass all 6. On the 12 differentiating cases, A fails exactly one CRITICAL check and B fails exactly one COSMETIC check — same per-case score (5/6), opposite meaning."
